## Thresholds

Owned by {{clean_code_link}} — when to split and into which pieces is decided there. Split by **responsibility**, not by line count.

<!-- GEN: Link the workspace's clean-code size/splitting reference; do NOT copy its numbers here (one source). Only if the workspace has no clean-code skill or doc: state the confirmed defaults here and say "until a clean-code skill exists". In the fullstack layout, link ../shared/splitting-with-clean-code.md for the protocol and keep only this branch's placement part and smell table. -->

## Division of roles

- **clean-code** decides *whether* to split, *into which pieces*, and what they are called.
- **clean-architecture** (this file) decides *where each piece goes* and keeps the dependency rule intact.

## Placement steps (this skill's half)

1. Take the pieces clean-code listed (one-line label each).
2. Run each label through the decision tree in `03-creating-files-folders.md` → target folder.
3. Choose the form: sibling file / whitelisted subfolder / another layer of the same module / shared (only when the dependency rules allow it).
4. Move the code, update every caller and test, delete the old code — no re-export shim.
5. Run: {{verify_commands}}

